35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"My findings suggest that narrow, focused tools survive, while broad, mandatory systems fade. We should seek a modest, sustainable solution.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I found that the capital budget is frozen... but the software allowance has some room. However, the per-head licenses are very expensive.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Sakura,,Oh no! I found out that the network at the plants is super spotty! It's like a game of hide-and-seek with the internet!,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The data is clear. We are losing hours every day to redundant copying and misrouted deliveries due to inconsistent records. This is a systemic waste.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The situation is worse than I thought. Our developers are fully booked, and the coordination group is severely understaffed. We cannot afford a high-maintenance project.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, your report confirms my fear. A complex project will collapse under its own weight if there is no one to tend the garden.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"If we use the software allowance, we might be okay... but if the license costs grow every year, we'll be in trouble next year.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Ryuji, if the records are messy, maybe it's because the internet keeps disappearing! How can you save a file if the signal goes poof?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, the misrouted deliveries are caused by different units having different data, not just signal loss. It is a failure of standardization.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, if the solution to that waste requires a new system, who will build it? We have no available developers and a broken coordination group.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"Let us remember that a small seed, well-watered, grows stronger than a giant tree planted in a storm. We need a low-maintenance fix.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think we should avoid anything with high recurring license fees. Fixed-fee work is much safer for our future budget.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Sakura,,I also saw that we keep asking vendors for the same things over and over! We're like goldfish! We forget everything!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"The waste is tangible. An hour a day per office is a massive loss. We must prioritize the proposal that eliminates this specific, daily friction.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,I will only support a proposal that does not require additional developer hours or more work for the coordination group. We are at a breaking point.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Servas,,"It seems we are in agreement on the constraints: low cost, low maintenance, and narrow scope. Let us see which candidate fits this mold.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
