60,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Candidate A seems the most sustainable. It addresses the standardization I found lacking and focuses on a specific, narrow data problem.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,Candidate A is a repository... that sounds like it might be a fixed-fee setup rather than a per-user license. It feels safer.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Sakura,,No way to Candidate D! I told you the internet at the plants is terrible! The app would just be a fancy brick!,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Candidate A is the only one that directly solves the misrouted deliveries and the time lost to copying records. It targets the actual floor-level waste.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Candidate B would put more pressure on the coordination group to manage the tool. Candidate A is a catalog; it is passive and requires less active maintenance.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, exactly. A catalog is a map. Once drawn, it serves many without requiring a guide to walk with them every day.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think A is the most conservative choice. It doesn't seem like it would create a huge bill for us next year.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Ryuji, if Candidate A stops us from asking vendors for the same things ten times, then I'm all for it! No more goldfish memories!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"It is the only logical choice. The other options are ""impressive"" in theory, but A solves the problems that are actually costing us time and money.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,Candidate C would require a production team we don't have. Candidate A is the only one that doesn't assume we have free staff to run it.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,"It is rare to see such harmony. We have looked at the past, the present, and the limits of our strength. The path is clear.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I feel... a bit more confident now. If everyone agrees it's low-risk, I'm happy to support it.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Sakura,,Yay! We solved the mystery! We're picking the one that doesn't need a magic internet signal to work!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,We are choosing based on evidence of waste rather than the appeal of the technology. This is the correct way to allocate the fund.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I am satisfied. Candidate A provides a solution without creating a new burden for the people who are already overworked.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Servas,,"Let us cast our votes. May this project be a small, sturdy bridge that lasts for many years to come.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
